		<div class="PostBody">
			<p itemprop="articleBody">
				<p><em><strong>In case anyone was wondering, USADA is still following Nick Diaz around…</strong></em></p><p><img src="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/06_1200_675575185606721781498828915.4147-696x365.jpg" alt="" title="06_1200_675575185606721781498828915.4147.jpg" height="365" width="696"></p><p>Former Strikeforce and WEC welterweight 
champion Nick Diaz is an interesting character. Outside his 
never-back-down style of fighting, Diaz’s unique and often highly 
entertaining trash talk makes him must watch TV.</p><p>Unfortunately since joining the UFC, Diaz’s career has faced
 multiple hurdles. One such incident involved the Nevada Athletic 
Commission slamming him with a five year ban. The punishment for 
Marijuana was later reduced to 18 months after widespread appeals.</p><p>This time around it’s USADA handing out the punishment, and Diaz might well never fight again as a result.</p><figure><a href="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/Nick-Diaz-Snoop-Dogg.jpg"><img src="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/Nick-Diaz-Snoop-Dogg-1024x576.jpg" alt="" height="360" width="640"></a>
<figcaption>Too much hanging around with Snoop?<br><br></figcaption></figure><h3><strong>Diaz Flagged by USADA</strong></h3><p>Some time ago we saw Diaz trolling a USADA tester as they 
tried to obtain a sample from his at 2 AM in Los Angeles. Well, it would
 now appear that USADA is not happy with Nick Diaz, who is supposed to 
make his whereabouts known at all times for USADA to test him.</p><p>It’s well known that the Diaz brothers 
don’t often go with the grain, and now Nick has caught a suspension 
pending further investigation. As far as USADA is concerned, they will 
likely view a failure to submit samples as equal to failing a test.</p><p>Here’s the statement:</p><p><a href="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/nate-diaz-nick-diaz-5822891.jpg"><img src="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/nate-diaz-nick-diaz-5822891.jpg" alt="" height="413" width="620"></a></p><h3><strong>USADA Suspends Diaz Pending Further Investigations</strong></h3><blockquote><p>“The UFC organization has been notified 
that the U.S. Anti-Doping Agency (USADA) has informed Nick Diaz of a 
potential Anti-Doping Policy violation stemming from Diaz’s alleged 
accumulation of three Whereabouts Failures within a 12-month period. 
Diaz, like all other UFC athletes, is enrolled in USADA’s UFC Registered
 Testing Pool and required to file accurate Whereabouts information in 
order to be located for out-of-competition, no-notice testing.</p><p>USADA, the independent 
administrator of the UFC Anti-Doping Policy, will handle the results 
management and appropriate adjudication of Diaz’s case, who has been 
provisionally suspended pending the final resolution of this matter. 
Under the UFC Anti-Doping Policy, there is a full and fair legal process
 that is afforded to all athletes before any sanctions are imposed. 
Additional information will be provided at the appropriate time as the 
process moves forward.”</p></blockquote><p>According to UFC president Dana White, chances are Diaz will never fight again anyway, regardless of this new drama:</p><figure><a href="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dana-white-ufc-fight-night.jpg"><img src="../../../cdn.scrapdigest.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/dana-white-ufc-fight-night.jpg" alt="" height="600" width="1000"></a>
<figcaption>Feb
 4, 2017; Houston, TX, USA; UFC president Dana White in attendance 
during UFC Fight Night at Toyota Center. Mandatory Credit: Mark J. 
Rebilas-USA TODAY Sports</figcaption></figure><h3><strong>Dana Not Hopeful</strong></h3><blockquote><p>&nbsp;I highly doubt it,” White told <a href="http://mmajunkie.com/2017/06/dana-white-i-dont-think-nick-diaz-will-ever-fight-again">MMAjunkie</a>.
 “I don’t know, I honestly don’t think that, and I can’t speak for him, 
you’d have to speak with Nick himself, but if you ask me – people ask 
me, ‘Do you think Ronda (Rousey) is coming back?’ No. I think Ronda’s 
going to retire. Ronda hasn’t retired, but my opinion is, I think she 
will. I don’t think Nick Diaz will ever fight again. I just don’t think 
he has the desire anymore.”</p><p>“The thing about 
fighting, first of all, it’s a young man’s game,” White said. “You’ve 
got to be young, hungry. You’ve got to be an animal to jump out of bed 
every day and go in there and train the way that you do.</p><p>“The things that you have to do to get to 
the UFC, let alone break into the top 10 or the top 5 or be a world 
champion, you have to love it. I just don’t think that Nick loves it 
anymore.”</p></blockquote><p><strong>Source:</strong><a href="http://www.scrapdigest.com/nick-diaz-suspended-usada-anti-doping-violation/20640/?utm_source=dlvr.it&amp;utm_medium=george%20st-pierre%20fanpage"><br></a></p><p><a href="http://www.scrapdigest.com/nick-diaz-suspended-usada-anti-doping-violation/20640/?utm_source=dlvr.it&amp;utm_medium=george%20st-pierre%20fanpage">http://www.scrapdigest.com/nick-diaz-suspended-usa...</a></p><p style="text-align: center;"></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 20px;"><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 0);"><br></span></span></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 20px;"><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">CLICK OUR HOMEPAGE TO PURCHASE BODYBUILDING SUPPLEMENTS!!</span></span></strong></p><p style="text-align: center; margin-left: 20px;"><a href="http://www.gymntonic.com/">GYM n TONIC Supplements <br></a></p>
			</p>
